# Single-line returns

When a function body is only a returned expression, write an arrow function and use its implicit return.

```ts
// Bad
export function createId() {
  return uuidv4();
}

// Good
export const createId = () => uuidv4();
```

When the expression is an object, wrap it in parentheses: `() => ({ id: uuidv4() })`.

When an `if` body is only a `return`, drop the braces.

```ts
// Bad
if (existing) {
  return { lines };
}

// Good
if (existing) return { lines };

if (!existing) return {
  lines: [...lines, { id: createId(), productId, quantity }],
};
```

Keep a block when the function or `if` does more than return. Do not convert class methods.
